INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction: The Importance of Smart Water Management in Large Farms</h2>\n<p>Given the constraints on water resources and the expansion of agricultural land in Iran, water conservation has become a primary challenge for farmers. Drip irrigation and micro-sprinkler systems, as the most advanced water delivery methods, enable the precise application of water and nutrients to the plant root zone. However, merely installing an irrigation system does not ensure high efficiency; proper management of pressure, flow rate, and irrigation scheduling plays a vital role in <strong>improving the efficiency of drip irrigation</strong> systems. In these sections, we will examine technical and managerial strategies to optimize the performance of these systems in extensive farms. The objective of this guide is to enable farmers to maximize the return on their investment in irrigation systems through a deep understanding of technical principles and to prevent the waste of vital resources. This is particularly critical as energy and consumable costs have increased. Consequently, focusing on precision in design, installation, and maintenance ensures the long-term survival and profitability of farms.</p>\n\n<h2>Key Strategies in the Precision Irrigation Guide</h2>\n<h3>Optimizing Pressure and Flow Rate in Large-Scale Systems</h3>\n<p>One of the biggest mistakes in large farms is ignoring pressure loss in long pipeline lines. To maintain uniform drip emitter output, pressure regulators and pumps with adequate power must be used. Pressure fluctuations lead to uneven water distribution and cause root stress in parts of the farm. Preliminary hydraulic calculations before installation guarantee uniform system performance at all points on the farm. Additionally, selecting the appropriate pipe diameter based on the distance from the main head to the point of use prevents a phenomenon known as \'Nori effect,\' where pressure drops at the end of the line. Farmers should know that the longer the line, the greater the need for mainline zoning or increased pipe diameters to prevent yield reduction in the far ends of the farm.</p>\n<h3>Choosing the right method: Drip or ribbon tape?</h3>\n<p>The choice between the two methods depends on crop type and soil. For <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%81%D8%A7%D8%B5%D9%84%D9%87-%D9%86%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%AA%DB%8C%D9%BE-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%DA%86%D8%BA%D9%86%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%82%D9%86%D8%AF-%D8%A8%D9%87%D8%AA%D8%B1%DB%8C%D9%86/">ribbon tape spacing in several sugar better</a>The distance between ribbon lines must be synchronized with the plant planting spacing. Conversely, drip systems are more suitable for tree and shrub crops with wide planting distances. Accurately understanding the differences between these two methods and how to select the best option for each farm is the first step in improving the system. For example, in dense-row vegetable farming, ribbon tape can increase irrigation speed and reduce equipment costs, whereas in pistachio and date orchards, drip systems take precedence due to the need for precise feeding and root moisture control.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/افزایش-بازدهی-آبیاری-قطرهای-در-مزارع-بزرگ-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="افزایش بازدهی آبیاری قطره‌ای در مزارع بزرگ - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>strategic irrigation guide</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h3>Integration with pressurized irrigation systems</h3>\n<p>For high-altitude farms where access to surface water sources is difficult, the use of powerful pumping units is critical. Study <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%87%D9%85%D9%87-%DA%86%DB%8C%D8%B2-%D8%AF%D8%B1%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%B1%D9%87-%D8%A2%D8%A8%DB%8C%D8%A7%D8%B1%DB%8C-%D8%B2%DB%8C%D8%B1%D8%B3%D8%B7%D8%AD%DB%8C/">Everything about subsurface irrigation</a> It offers a new perspective on the uniform distribution of moisture in the soil profile, which promotes deeper root growth and increases plant tolerance to drought stress. Subsurface irrigation significantly improves water use efficiency by reducing direct evaporation from the soil surface. In arid and desert regions with high evaporation rates, this method can reduce total agricultural water consumption by up to 30 percent.</p>\n\n<h2>Practical tips for increasing yield and reducing costs</h2>\n<p>After system installation, daily operation and maintenance determine the final performance. Adhering to the following principles minimizes losses caused by emitter clogging and water waste:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Precise filtration:</strong> Using disc or sand filters with the appropriate grade prevents fine particles from entering the emitters. Regular filter cleaning is essential. When using brackish or saline wells, installing multi-stage filters is necessary to ensure complete sediment removal.</li>\n<li><strong>Fertigation:</strong> Simultaneously applying fertilizer and water ensures nutrients are available precisely in the root zone. This practice increases nutrient uptake efficiency by up to 30 percent, reduces fertilizer transport costs, and prevents nutrient leaching from the soil surface.</li>\n<li><strong>Scheduling irrigation based on crop requirements:</strong> Using sensors or soil moisture probes instead of fixed timers prevents overwatering. Monitoring soil moisture at root depth increases system accuracy and prevents root damage from waterlogging or drying out.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For dryland and rainfed farms, which are highly sensitive to water management, knowing <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%DB%8C%D8%B2%D8%A7%D9%86-%D8%A8%D8%B1%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B4%D8%AA-%D8%AC%D9%88-%D8%AF%D9%88%D8%B3%D8%B1-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/">the barley yield per hectare</a> and how irrigation affects it can help farmers determine the optimal irrigation level for their specific crop. Additionally, for some crops like potatoes, familiarity with <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/potato-yield-per-hectare-increase-methods/">potato yield per hectare increase methods</a> indicates that uniform irrigation leads to uniform potato sizing and improved commercial quality. Uniformity in crop size directly impacts harvesting labor costs and final selling prices.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/افزایش-بازدهی-آبیاری-قطرهای-در-مزارع-بزرگ-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="افزایش بازدهی آبیاری قطره‌ای در مزارع بزرگ - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>strategic irrigation guide</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) About Drip Irrigation in Large Farms</h2>\n<h3>1. Is drip irrigation suitable for all crops?</h3>\n<p>No. Crops with very close planting spacing, such as some leafy greens, are better suited for tape emitters. However, for fruit trees, corn, tomatoes, and potatoes, drip is generally more efficient. The correct choice also depends on soil type, land slope, and air temperature.</p>\n<h3>2. How often should emitters be cleaned?</h3>\n<p>In systems with clean water sources, annual cleaning is sufficient. However, if you use saline wells or surface water sources, they must be carefully washed every 3 to 6 months using trichlor or citric acid. Washing must be performed when the pump is off and outlet valves are open to ensure the wash flow passes completely through the system.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/افزایش-بازدهی-آبیاری-قطرهای-در-مزارع-بزرگ-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="افزایش بازدهی آبیاری قطره‌ای در مزارع بزرگ - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>strategic irrigation guide</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h3>3. How do we prevent line clogging caused by calcium deposits?</h3>\n<p>Inject acidifying compounds into the system using a fertigation pump. Additionally, avoid using alkaline solutions with standard plastic emitters. Maintaining the pH of water entering the system within the range of 6 to 8 prevents precipitation of solutes inside the pipes.</p>\n\n<h2>Conclusion and Next Steps</h2>\n<p>Improving drip irrigation efficiency in large farms requires a comprehensive approach beyond simply purchasing equipment. This process includes precise hydraulic design, appropriate filtration selection, and intelligent plant nutrition management. Implementing these measures not only reduces water consumption but also improves final crop yield due to reduced water stress and increased nutrient uptake. To better understand the principles of proper installation, studying <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/qadamhoi-nasbi-navori-tip/">qadamhoi nasbi navori tip</a> can be a good guide for resolving potential issues. Ultimately, regular monitoring of system performance and soil moisture is the key to maintaining your long-term investment. Farmers should remember that an irrigation system is a living entity that requires continuous interpretation and attention to reach its peak efficiency.</p>','Increasing Drip Irrigation Efficiency in Large-Scale Farms: Strategic and Practical Guide','In this useful article, we examine practical and strategic solutions to improve the efficiency of drip irrigation in large farms. With a focus on tape and drip systems, you will learn how to reduce costs and improve crop performance through proper resource management.','publish','closed','closed','increasing-drip-irrigation-efficiency-large-scale-farms',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
